{
  "slug": "miro",
  "name": "Miro",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Secure access to Miro boards. Enables AI to read board context, create diagrams, and generate code with enterprise-grade security.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 skills** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (7): `miro-browse` (Use when the user wants to explore, list, summarize, or inspect items on a Miro board), `miro-code-explain-on-board` (Use when the user wants to explain or visualize a codebase on a Miro board — produces a…), `miro-code-review` (Use when the user wants to create a visual code review on a Miro board from a pull/merge…), `miro-code-spec` (Use when the user wants to extract a Miro board's specs (documents, diagrams, prototypes, tables, frames, images) to…), `miro-diagram` (Use when the user wants to create or update a diagram on a Miro board), `miro-doc` (Use when the user wants to create or edit a Google-Docs-style markdown document on a Miro board), `miro-table` (Use when the user wants to create or update a structured table on a Miro board)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `miro`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install miro@claude-plugins-official` from `miroapp/miro-ai` (`claude-plugins/miro`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
